job_description:
[RESPONSIBILITIES]

1.Support data analysts in the China region to prepare and process primary data;
2.Generate key slides for customer experience reports;
3.Collaborate with data analysts on the creation of analysis;
4. Manage project timelines and delivery for assigned missions;
5. Proofreading and data checking research reports to ensure deliverables are error-free;
6. You will query directly the data from Snowflake with your knowledge in SQL to provide analysis to analysts.

[REQUIREMENTS]
1.1 to 2 years’ experience working with data;
2.Passionate towards the Luxury and Fashion industry;
3. Detail-orientated, fast learner, good time management and able to work in a fast-paced work environment with a can-do attitude;
4. Able to interpret large/small amounts of data and multi-task;
5. Strong communication skills;
6. Strong analytical mind and critical thinking skills;
7. Excellent knowledge in MS Office (Excel, Word, PowerPoint);
8.Skills in Power BI, SQL, R, Python or automation tool is a plus;
9.Exceptional written, oral communication abilities in English and Chinese;
10. Preferably from Statistics, Marketing, Psychology or Economics background;
11. 1 to 2 years’ experience working with data.

Friendly with working remotely, pay rate to be discussed.
